  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts` and it passes `typecheck`. I haven't run `vite build` or loaded it in a browser, so the rendering, the orbit drag and `__EVAL_READY__` are untested.\n\n- **Cube and material:** one 1.7-unit cube using `material.pbr` (metallic 0.9, roughness 0.38, steel-grey).\n- **Lighting and background:** a neutral image-based environment for reflections, a hemisphere fill, and warm key, cool fill and white rim directional lights. The background is dark grey (`#2a2a2e`).\n- **Rotation:** the cube spins on all three axes. It is driven each frame by an `app.onFrame` callback that sets its rotation on the runtime node handle. This assumes the angle is in radians, which I inferred from the engine code rather than confirmed.\n- **Orbit control:** `interactions.orbit()` in this engine only records that orbit is enabled and does no dragging. I mounted the orbit camera rig from `camera.rigs.orbit` and wired canvas pointer events to its `dragBy`. This works while the cube keeps spinning. The rig has no typed `dragBy`, so I cast it to a small local interface.\n- **Framing:** the orbit rig is aimed at the origin with a 40° field of view at distance 6.4, so the whole cube should be centred.\n- **Canvas and ready flag:** the app draws into the existing `canvas#app` with `resize: false` and `pixelRatio: 1`. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set one animation frame after the first frame callback.\n\n",
